      "semantic_checks": [
        "AtMiss requires an actual absent seed slot and the complete preceding sampler executes before the fresh pair draw. The old state may contain arbitrary prior keys or aliases; no independence of existing sessions is assumed.",
        "The split equivalence preserves both complete32 halves. False selects seed.1, true seed.2, and kernel_inputs ties these to both concrete physical send/receive source fields.",
        "realize_mask restores the exact World.resolve kernel, full seed cache, lookup/draw counts, uniform+64 and all other World fields. miss_continuation quantifies over the complete reply/poststate continuation.",
        "observed_delayed hides the newly chosen32 from the entire masked observer and delays that actual sample. seedAt fallback is removed by the actual cacheQuery_self proof at the miss. No whole-source target-freeness assumption occurs.",
        "candidate_bound is an unconditioned supported-list bound, including repetitions, with explicit qCandidates/2^256 and no hidden success, slot, or role loss.",
        "first_source samples all prior context and opposite32 inside unitObserver; the primitive input sampler is the existing ordinary Unit-context uniform32 endpoint. The full continuation draw-order equality is explicit.",
        "first_bound has only SourceFullCorrect as its functional premise and displays one Extract and one HMAC advantage, each coefficient one. No H7 forbidden source use or new related-key/public-context assumption occurs.",
        "The component firstReal explicitly computes the actual source function after resolve. Its join to a reached native callback and native counter update is left to the global compiler, as documented.",
        "Uniform query bounds include complete seed64, retained32, qSample/qObserve, unused input32, real HMAC key64, and both complete random64 replies. HMAC challenge cap is two."
      ],
